  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 115 AM CDT Wed May 27 2026\n\nThe upper low over the west will begin to lift out toward the \nnortheast Friday and bring southwesterly flow over TX for the \nweekend. The low level flow will continue to be from the southeast. \nThis will bring a warm, moist airmass over our CWA. A series of \nupper level shortwaves will bring chances for showers and \nthunderstorms each afternoon Saturday through Tuesday. At this time \nnothing looks well organized, strong, or heavy rain producing. We \nwill see what later forecasts show.",
